xraylib
------------------------------------------
This is xraylib, a library for X-ray matter interactions cross sections for
X-ray fluorescence applications: core C library

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgfortran5-14.4.0-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libxrl-devel-4.3.0-1bl1
  libxrl11-4.3.0-1bl1
  libxrlf03-devel-4.3.0-1bl1
  libxrlf03_11-4.3.0-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1
  python312-3.12.12-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  meson-1.10.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  python3-3.12.12-1
  python3-devel-3.12.12-1
  python312-numpy-2.5.4-1
  swig-4.5.1-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/tschoonj/xraylib

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/tschoonj/xraylib/archive/refs/tags/xraylib-4.3.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack xraylib-4.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./xraylib-4.3.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/xraylib-4.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/xraylib-4.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libxrl11-4.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libxrl-devel-4.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libxrlf03_11-4.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libxrlf03-devel-4.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/python312-xraylib-4.3.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

